# --- 2.2 Evaluation and proofs ---

uslng:c-eval
    a spp:Component ;
    rdfs:label "usl-ng-eval"@en ;
    spp:componentName "usl-ng-eval" ;
    spp:moduleRole sppc:mr-application ;
    spp:declaredDependency uslng:dep-thiserror ,
                           uslng:dep-miette .
    # Pass 3 refinement: re-classified from mr-utility → mr-application.
    # The crate's own Cargo.toml description (verbatim): "Denotational
    # interpreter for USL-NG LInvExpr: evaluates §7 predicate
    # expressions against an environment of bound values." That is
    # application-layer behaviour over the §4 AST, not a generic
    # utility. The crate is also the host of the REPL module
    # (src/repl.rs, ~23 KB) and the runtime value model (src/value.rs);
    # the README at crates/usl-ng-eval/README.md ratifies its scope.
    #
    # Internal-workspace deps (usl-ng-ast, usl-ng-parser) are excluded
    # from declaredDependency per the §2.3 rule and instead surface as
    # link-eval-depends-on-ast and link-eval-depends-on-parser in §5.

uslng:c-proofs
    a spp:Component ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 mechanization (proofs/)"@en ;
    spp:componentName "proofs" ;
    spp:moduleRole sppc:mr-domain .
    # The proof tree is part of the product per PURPOSE.md §"Math is
    # part of the product"; it is not an adjunct artifact.
    # Ground-truth verification (commit 293d08d):
    #   - proofs/lean-toolchain pins `leanprover/lean4:v4.12.0`.
    #   - proofs/lake-manifest.json declares zero packages
    #     (`"packages": []`) — no Mathlib, no other deps. This is the
    #     mechanical realisation of adr-no-mathlib.
    #   - proofs/USLNG/ contains 17 Lean modules (Conjecture_6_3,
    #     Conjecture_6_7_5, Core, Demo, EditSet, Feat, FeatBridge, I0,
    #     Lens, LensZodJsonSchema, NgLensPair, Partial, PathBSig,
    #     Prop1_6, Shalens, Theorems, ZodFull, ZodMoney) plus the root
    #     USLNG.lean — counts and module list per the run snapshot;
    #     theorem and `sorry` counts are claimed by README.md (222
    #     theorems, 0 sorry) and are not separately verified here.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2.4 Self-describing artefacts (canonical/)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo ships its own project-plan artefacts under canonical/:
#   - canonical/software-project-plan.ttl: the SHACL/TTL ontology +
#     shapes graph this instance validates against.
#   - canonical/usl-ng-plan.ttl: an in-tree copy of *this* plan,
#     validated by scripts/validate_plan_ttl.py (regression in
#     scripts/test_validate_plan_ttl.py).
#   - canonical/README.md: human-facing companion documentation.
#   - canonical/tests/pyproject.toml + uv.lock: a uv-managed Python
#     environment for running pyshacl against the plan.
# These are deliberately not modelled as spp:Component nodes because
# they are *artefacts of the plan itself*, not parts of the running
# software product. They are recorded here as ground-truth context so
# that a reader can locate the source-of-truth for the schema and the
# in-tree instance.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2.3 Declared workspace dependencies
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed: every dependency named in [workspace.dependencies] of the
# root Cargo.toml (verified 2026-05-15 against commit 293d08d).
#
# Not listed:
#   - Transitive dependencies (resolver's responsibility, not
#     plan-time declaration).
#   - Per-crate dev-dependencies (proptest 1.9 in usl-ng-parser,
#     usl-ng-printer, usl-ng-semantic; `syn` in usl-ng-ast for the §4
#     spec-schema-sync test) — those belong to test-time, which is
#     covered by spp:testTechnique tt-property-based above.
#   - Per-crate dependencies declared *directly* against crates.io
#     rather than through [workspace.dependencies]. Today this is just
#     usl-ng-cli's `notify = "6.1"` and `rustyline = "14"`. These are
#     noted in c-cli's commentary rather than promoted to first-class
#     Dependency entities, to preserve the invariant that
#     spp:Dependency nodes mirror [workspace.dependencies] one-for-one.
#   - Intra-workspace path dependencies (every `usl_ng_* = { path =
#     "..." }` line) — those are graph edges between in-tree
#     components and surface as spp:PlannedLink in §5, not as
#     spp:Dependency in §2.3.
#
# Workspace-wide Rust environment (root Cargo.toml [workspace.package]):
# `edition = "2021"`, `rust-version = "1.75"`, `resolver = "2"`. There
# is no SPP predicate for these today; recorded here as ground-truth
# provenance for the spp:runtimePlatform rt-rust declaration above.

